\n. 2020 Mar;79(3):408-417.\n\ndoi: 10.1136/annrheumdis-2019-215926. Epub 2019 Dec 23.\n\n### Authors\n\n[Hao Sun](/?term=Sun+H&cauthor_id=31871141) [#](#short-view-equal-contrib-explanation \"Contributed equally\")  [1](#short-view-affiliation-1 \"Department of Orthopedics, Sun Yat-Sen Memorial Hospital, Guangzhou, China.\")   [2](#short-view-affiliation-2 \"Department of Joint Surgery, Sun Yat-sen University First Affiliated Hospital, Guangzhou, China.\") , [Xingzhao Wen](/?term=Wen+X&cauthor_id=31871141) [#](#short-view-equal-contrib-explanation \"Contributed equally\")  [2](#short-view-affiliation-2 \"Department of Joint Surgery, Sun Yat-sen University First Affiliated Hospital, Guangzhou, China.\") , [Hongyi Li](/?term=Li+H&cauthor_id=31871141)  [2](#short-view-affiliation-2 \"Department of Joint Surgery, Sun Yat-sen University First Affiliated Hospital, Guangzhou, China.\") , [Peihui Wu](/?term=Wu+P&cauthor_id=31871141)  [2](#short-view-affiliation-2 \"Department of Joint Surgery, Sun Yat-sen University First Affiliated Hospital, Guangzhou, China.\") , [Minghui Gu](/?term=Gu+M&cauthor_id=31871141)  [2](#short-view-affiliation-2 \"Department of Joint Surgery, Sun Yat-sen University First Affiliated Hospital, Guangzhou, China.\") , [Xiaoyi Zhao](/?term=Zhao+X&cauthor_id=31871141)  [2](#short-view-affiliation-2 \"Department of Joint Surgery, Sun Yat-sen University First Affiliated Hospital, Guangzhou, China.\") , [Ziji Zhang](/?term=Zhang+Z&cauthor_id=31871141)  [2](#short-view-affiliation-2 \"Department of Joint Surgery, Sun Yat-sen University First Affiliated Hospital, Guangzhou, China.\") , [Shu Hu](/?term=Hu+S&cauthor_id=31871141)  [2](#short-view-affiliation-2 \"Department of Joint Surgery, Sun Yat-sen University First Affiliated Hospital, Guangzhou, China.\") , [Guping Mao](/?term=Mao+G&cauthor_id=31871141)  [2](#short-view-affiliation-2 \"Department of Joint Surgery, Sun Yat-sen University First Affiliated Hospital, Guangzhou, China.\") , [Ruofan Ma](/?term=Ma+R&cauthor_id=31871141)  [1](#short-view-affiliation-1 \"Department of Orthopedics, Sun Yat-Sen Memorial Hospital, Guangzhou, China.\") , [Weiming Liao](/?term=Liao+W&cauthor_id=31871141)  [3](#short-view-affiliation-3 \"Department of Joint Surgery, Sun Yat-sen University First Affiliated Hospital, Guangzhou, China zhzhiqi@mail.sysu.edu.cn liaowmsysu@163.com.\") , [Zhiqi Zhang](/?term=Zhang+Z&cauthor_id=31871141)  [3](#short-view-affiliation-3 \"Department of Joint Surgery, Sun Yat-sen University First Affiliated Hospital, Guangzhou, China zhzhiqi@mail.sysu.edu.cn liaowmsysu@163.com.\")\n\n### Affiliations\n\n-   1 Department of Orthopedics, Sun Yat-Sen Memorial Hospital, Guangzhou, China.\n-   2 Department of Joint Surgery, Sun Yat-sen University First Affiliated Hospital, Guangzhou, China.\n-   3 Department of Joint Surgery, Sun Yat-sen University First Affiliated Hospital, Guangzhou, China zhzhiqi@mail.sysu.edu.cn liaowmsysu@163.com.\n\n# Contributed equally.\n\n-   PMID: **31871141**\n-   PMCID: [PMC7034356](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7034356/)\n-   DOI: [10.1136/annrheumdis-2019-215926](https://doi.org/10.1136/annrheumdis-2019-215926)\n\nItem in Clipboard\n\nFull text links Cite\n\nDisplay options\n\nDisplay options\n\nFormat AbstractPubMedPMID\n\n## Abstract\n\n**Objectives:** The heterogeneity of meniscus cells and the mechanism of meniscus degeneration is not well understood. Here, single-cell RNA sequencing (scRNA-seq) was used to identify various meniscus cell subsets and investigate the mechanism of meniscus degeneration.\n\n**Methods:** scRNA-seq was used to identify cell subsets and their gene signatures in healthy human and degenerated meniscus cells to determine their differentiation relationships and characterise the diversity within specific cell types. Colony-forming, multi-differentiation assays and a mice meniscus injury model were used to identify meniscus progenitor cells. We investigated the role of degenerated meniscus progenitor (DegP) cell clusters during meniscus degeneration using computational analysis and experimental verification.\n\n**Results:** We identified seven clusters in healthy human meniscus, including five empirically defined populations and two novel populations. Pseudotime analysis showed endothelial cells and fibrochondrocyte progenitors (FCP) existed at the pseudospace trajectory start. Melanoma cell adhesion molecule ((MCAM)/CD146) was highly expressed in two clusters. CD146+ meniscus cells differentiated into osteoblasts and adipocytes and formed colonies. We identified changes in the proportions of degenerated meniscus cell clusters and found a cluster specific to degenerative meniscus with progenitor cell characteristics. The reconstruction of four progenitor cell clusters indicated that FCP differentiation into DegP was an aberrant process. Interleukin 1β stimulation in healthy human meniscus cells increased CD318+ cells, while TGFβ1 attenuated the increase in CD318+ cells in degenerated meniscus cells.\n\n**Conclusions:** The identification of meniscus progenitor cells provided new insights into cell-based meniscus tissue engineering, demonstrating a novel mechanism of meniscus degeneration, which contributes to the development of a novel therapeutic strategy.\n\n**Keywords:** arthritis; cytokines; fibroblasts.\n\n© Author(s) (or their employer(s)) 2020. Re-use permitted under CC BY. Published by BMJ.\n\n[PubMed Disclaimer](/disclaimer/)\n\n## Conflict of interest statement\n\nCompeting interests: None declared.\n\n## Figures\n\n [![Figure 1](https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/blobs/72cd/7034356/f04269c26310/annrheumdis-2019-215926f01.gif)](https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/blobs/72cd/7034356/d8a455138590/annrheumdis-2019-215926f01.jpg) \n\n**\n\nFigure 1\n\n**\n\nA single-cell atlas of healthy…\n\n**\n\nFigure 1\n\n**\n\nA single-cell atlas of healthy human meniscus. (A) Seven healthy human meniscus cell…\n\n**Figure 1**\n\nA single-cell atlas of healthy human 