ron in the neocortex with a confidence of 0.724125093 (NS-Forest FBeta value).\")\n35046: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4072036 \"PAX6 GABAergic interneuron (Homo sapiens)\")\n35047: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4072036 obo:CL_4042032)\n35048: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4072036 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_9606))\n35049: SubClassOf(obo:CL_4072036 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0015004 obo:CLM_1000079))\n35050: \n35051: # Class: obo:CL_4072037 (L2/3 intratelencephalic projecting glutamatergic neuron (Homo sapiens))\n35052: \n35053: AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000028 obo:CL_4072037 \"L2/3 IT (Homo sapiens)\")\n35054: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25622573\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34004146\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37292694\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/c3aa4f95-7a18-4a7d-8dd8-ca324d714363.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4072037 \"A transcriptomically distinct intratelencephalic-projecting glutamatergic neuron with a soma found between cortical layer 2-4. This intratelencephalic-projecting glutamatergic neuron has thin-tufted apical dendrites and extends its axonal projection into L5 in the neocortex. This neuronal type has a hyperpolarised resting membrane potential. The standard transcriptomic reference data for this cell type can be found on the CellxGene census under the collection: 'Transcriptomic cytoarchitecture reveals principles of human neocortex organization', dataset: 'Supercluster: IT-projecting excitatory neurons', Author Categories: 'CrossArea_subclass', clusters L2/3 IT.\")\n35055: AnnotationAssertion(obo:RO_0002175 obo:CL_4072037 obo:NCBITaxon_9606)\n35056: AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4072037 \"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5507-2103\")\n35057: AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4072037 \"2025-09-10T09:15:51Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n35058: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_4072037